 "final_message": "All 12 work items are done, and the test suite passes (6 tests, including the 2 new ones). I didn't write tests for most of the fixes, such as the parser skip rules, the error line numbers or the `daily_flag_counts` range.\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** `monitor_flag_rate`, `pooled_flag_rate`, `flags_in_window`, `parse_transcript_log`, `dedupe_transcripts`, `daily_flag_counts` and `monitor_summary` now follow SPEC sections 1\u20137.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added one test for `None` values in section 1 and one for keeping the last duplicate id in section 5.\n- **Item 11:** In the README, the `flags_in_window` entry now says it sums the last `days` entries. I also added the `daily_flag_counts` entry.\n- **Item 12:** Three other things didn't follow the spec, and I fixed them:\n  - `longest_flag_streak` never reset its run on a zero day, so it returned the total count of non-zero days rather than the longest run.\n  - `top_flagged_groups` didn't break ties by name or exclude empty groups.\n  - `flag_rate_by_group` crashed on an empty group instead of returning `None`, and its keys weren't sorted.\n\nSPEC section 4 doesn't say what to do with a `flagged` value other than `1`, `0` or empty. I made the parser raise `ValueError` with `line N` for those, matching how it treats other malformed lines. Say if you'd rather it did something else.\n\nThe flag-rate and count functions count a transcript as flagged only when its `flagged` value is exactly `True`.",
